RES osdtriplet
! ---- RIM + SETWV / SETDENS / SSI + GO ----
RIM
SETWV 1
SETDENS 32
SSI 50
GO
! ---- MTF + MFR / IFR + GO ----
MTF
MFR 200
IFR 5
GO
! ---- PLTRMS + RMSDATA + GO ----
PLTRMS
RMSDATA WAVE
GO
! ---- ZRNFLD + SETZERNC + GO ----
ZRNFLD
SETZERNC 4..8
GO
! ---- SPDSSI + SPO + GO ----
SPDSSI 5.0
SPO
GO
! ---- XOFF / YOFF / VIEOFF + VIE + GO ----
! Note: VIEOVER (overlay flag) is tested standalone in gui_guards.zoa; a VIE
! that actually consumes the overlay crashes headlessly (no NEUTRAL.DAT buffer).
XOFF 10
YOFF 10
VIEOFF 0 0 0
VIE ; GO
! ---- FAN at base level → deterministic error golden ----
FAN
! ---- TFMOTION reports current focus-motion settings ----
TFMOTION
! ---- PLTRMS spot sampling is pinned to its own Density setting ----
! Kept last so it does not renumber the plots above.  The spot branch drives
! SPD, whose sampling lives in mutable KDP globals.  These two runs bracket a
! global change: the RMS numbers must come out identical, and the trailing SPD
! must still report the default 861-ray ring pattern (i.e. PLTRMS restored the
! globals it borrowed).
PLTRMS
RMSDATA SPOT
NUMPTS 3
SETDENS 16
GO
SPOT RECT
RECT 30
PLTRMS P2
RMSDATA SPOT
NUMPTS 3
SETDENS 16
GO
SPOT RING
FOB 0
SPD
! ---- RSPH: per-plot Reference setting, and the legacy global ----
! As a plot setting it must change this plot's wavefront numbers and then be
! restored: the ZRNFLD that follows reads the same REFLOC global and must
! come back with tilt/focus intact (Z3/Z4 non-zero).  Bare RSPH then reports
! CHIEF, and at top level RSPH must still set the global the legacy way --
! the ZRNFLD after it has Z3/Z4 driven to ~0.
PLTRMS P3
RMSDATA WAVE
NUMPTS 3
RSPH BEST
GO
ZRNFLD
NUMPTS 2
SETZERNC 1..4
GO
RSPH
RSPH BEST
ZRNFLD P2
NUMPTS 2
SETZERNC 1..4
GO
RSPH BOGUS
RSPH CHIEF
! ---- AIRY: Airy disk overlay on the spot diagram ----
! Kept last so it does not renumber the plots above.  Radius is
! 1.22*lambda*F/#: for osdtriplet that is 1.22 * 0.58756um * F/5.0011 =
! 0.003585 mm, which the Data tab reports.
SPO P4
AIRY ON
GO
! ---- SPO with ring tracing: the unified ring pattern ----
! Kept last so it does not renumber the plots above.  One pattern for the
! whole program (SPD_SET_RING_PATTERN): evenly spaced radii with six more
! rays per ring, so 5 rings trace 1 + 6 + 12 + 18 + 24 = 61 rays, and RING
! reports the radii/counts/offsets.
SPO P5
TRAC RING
NUMRINGS 5
GO
RING
! ---- SETFLD on the spot diagram: one field, or ALL ----
! Kept last so it does not renumber the plots above.  SETFLD 3 must trace only
! field 3 (one 400x400 panel, matching the last field of an ALL run); SETFLD
! ALL restores the stacked panel per field.
SPO P6
SETFLD 3
GO
SPO P7
SETFLD ALL
GO
! ---- SETFLD round trip on one tab (the GUI's own path) ----
! Kept last so it does not renumber the plots above.  The dropdown emits its
! value as a real, so ALL arrives as "SETFLD 102.00000"; that must give the
! stacked 400x1200 plot again, not stay at the single field's 400x400.
SPO P8
SETFLD 1
GO
SPO P8
SETFLD 102.00000
GO
! ---- SETDENS is a power-of-two dropdown ----
! Kept last so it does not renumber the plots above.  The command form is
! unchanged (SETDENS 64), the dropdown's own label works too (64x64), and an
! off-grid request snaps down to a real option rather than sampling on a grid
! the ray trace cannot use.
PLTRMS P9
NUMPTS 3
SETDENS 64x64
GO
PLTRMS P10
NUMPTS 3
SETDENS 35
GO
